# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Env
# Match every .env variant rather than listing the ones we happen to use today.
# The relayer key is the whole system — it owns all four contracts, is the sole
# onlyRelayer address and pays all gas — and the deploy story involves a
# production env file, so `.env.production` or a stray `.env.bak` while editing
# is the one realistic way it reaches a commit. Committing it once is permanent:
# the repo is about to be public and deleting a file does not remove it from
# history. The example files are the deliberate exception; they hold only
# placeholders and are what tells a fresh clone which vars exist.
.env*
!.env.example

# Build outputs
.next/
dist/
out/

# Foundry
cache/
broadcast/

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.log

# Runtime caches
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.tsbuildinfo

.vercel
